  "title": "AI-Driven Cybersecurity Measures in India and Global Context",
  "summary": "Business Standard reports that telecom operators and strategic infrastructure providers are strengthening network security through discussions with telecom major entities to combat AI-led cyberattacks. Meanwhile, the Indian government is working on provisions to resolve issues with the Trai regulatory body over penalizing telecom operators for spam-related violations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Three to four rounds of discussions with telecom operators and infrastructure providers were held to enhance network security.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government is working on provisions to resolve Trai's ability to impose financial penalties on telecom operators for spam violations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "According to official data, grievances against spam calls and messages have been rising year-on-year since 2022.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
